 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Newsletter Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is newsletter automation?\", \"a\": \"Newsletter automation uses software tools and technologies to streamline and manage creating, sending, and tracking email newsletters. Beyond the send itself, it can cover drafting each issue from content you already publish and keeping the subscriber list current.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I set up newsletter automation?\", \"a\": \"Start with the steps you repeat for every issue, and give each one a trigger and an owner. With Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a>, you describe those steps in a prompt and get a working app with its own database. Run one past issue through it as a dry run before the first real send.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should newsletter automation software do besides schedule emails?\", \"a\": \"It should cover the work around the send: collecting content into a draft, routing it for approval, chasing sponsor deadlines, and keeping the list clean. A scheduler alone leaves an editor assembling each issue by hand. Check whether you can write your own rules or only pick templates. An app built on Emergent runs those rules with no task cap.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can newsletter automation handle sponsor bookings?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if each sponsor slot is kept as a record tied to an issue date, with the sponsor and the copy deadline on it. A booking form that reads those records offers only open dates, and a reminder goes out when copy is late. If you pitch larger packages with custom pricing, <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/proposal'>proposal automation</a> can draft and track those offers before a booking lands.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should newsletter automation do when a reader unsubscribes?\", \"a\": \"It should take the reader off every list at once and cancel any issue already scheduled for them. For commercial email, the FTC's CAN-SPAM guide says to honor a recipient's opt-out request within 10 business days. The same guide says any opt-out mechanism you offer must be able to process opt-out requests for at least 30 days after you send your message.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can newsletter automation send each reader different sections?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Store each reader's topic picks as tags in your email service, then build one issue whose sections show only to readers with the matching tag. Decide what a reader who picked nothing gets, such as every section, before the first send. Topic picks also sit in a database you own, where you can see which sections readers choose over time.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should I ask readers before setting up newsletter automation?\", \"a\": \"Ask which topics they want most, with a short <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/ranking'>ranking survey</a> that lists your current sections and a few new ideas. Each reader puts the topics in order, and the average rank shows which ones to lead with. Run it twice a year and compare the results with the links readers click.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can newsletter automation pull posts from a blog feed?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if your blog publishes a feed or has an API. The app checks the feed on a schedule, picks up every post newer than the last issue, and adds each one with its title and link. Keep the editor's approval step, since a feed also carries posts you may not want in an issue.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can newsletter automation handle reader submissions?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Give readers a submission form with a few fixed fields, such as a link and a one-line pitch. Each entry lands in a queue with a status the editor sets while building the issue. Emergent builds the form and the queue from a prompt, and you can add a field later by prompting.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I measure whether newsletter automation is working for readers?\", \"a\": \"Combine click data with a direct question about each issue. Clicks show which links got attention. A short <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/likert-questionnaire'>likert questionnaire</a> asks readers to rate a statement such as \\\"This issue saves me time\\\" on an agreement scale. Send it to a sample of readers twice a year and track the scores against open and click rates.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
  "alpb---prompt": "<p>Build newsletter automation that runs on its own and logs every step.</p><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbPrompt = {\"default\": \"Build newsletter automation that runs on its own and logs every step.\", \"chips\": [{\"label\": \"Weekly Drafts\", \"add\": \"Add weekly drafts that build each issue from the week's posts and saved links.\"}, {\"label\": \"Sponsor Slots\", \"add\": \"Add sponsor slots that track bookings per issue and chase late ad copy.\"}, {\"label\": \"Reader Topics\", \"add\": \"Add reader topics that pick the sections each subscriber gets.\"}, {\"label\": \"List Cleanup\", \"add\": \"Add list cleanup that re-confirms subscribers who stopped clicking.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
